aui 1
summary "The Rivian R2 is the more versatile, trail-ready package; the Tesla Model Y is the easier value choice today, with mature availability and charging. The better buy depends on whether utility or low-friction ownership matters more."
header 🚙 "At a glance" "Utility versus ease"
compare 🚙
col "Rivian R2" img:"rivian r2 press photo"
col "Tesla Model Y" img:"tesla model y press photo"
cgroup "Best for"
crow "Ideal owner" "Adventure and cargo" "Road trips and commuting"
crow "Availability" "New rollout" "On sale now" win:2 n1:"Wait likely" n2:"Buy now"
cgroup "Price and range"
crow "Starting price" "$45,000 est." "$41,630" win:2 n1:"Target price" n2:"Lower today"
crow "Maximum range" "345 mi est." "357 mi EPA" win:2 n1:"Strong range" n2:"Longest range"
cgroup "Performance"
crow "Quickest 0-60" "3.6 sec" "3.3 sec" win:2 n1:"Very quick" n2:"0.3s faster"
crow "Road character" "Rugged and tall" "Lower and sharper"
cgroup "Charging"
crow "Connector" "Native NACS" "Native NACS"
crow "Peak DC rate" "230 kW est." "250 kW" win:2 n1:"Lower peak" n2:"Higher peak"
cgroup "Space and utility"
crow "Ground clearance" "9.6 in" "6.6 in" win:1 n1:"Much higher" n2:"Road height"
crow "Total cargo" "90.1 cu ft" "76 cu ft" win:1 n1:"More space" n2:"Less space"
crow "Third row" "No" "Optional"
facts "What stands out"
item 🏔 "R2 feels more SUV" "Its clearance, boxier body, and storage favor trails, snow, and bulky cargo."
item ⚡ "Model Y is easier now" "It pairs a mature lineup with established delivery and charging infrastructure."
item 👨‍👩‍👧 "Different family tradeoff" "R2 prioritizes cargo; some Model Y trims trade space for optional third-row seats."
header 🎯 "My take"
intro "Choose the R2 when clearance, utility, and character justify waiting. Choose the Model Y when price, availability, and a proven ownership path matter most."
